---
// A guided first open-source contribution, practised on the antipaywall/ideas repo (one Markdown
// file per wanted tool), never on the platform's own code. Two ways: with a coding agent, or in
// the browser on GitHub with nothing to install. The page fills in the file and the agent prompt
// from what the person types; it remembers their place in this browser only.
import Platform from '../layouts/Platform.astro';

const REPO = 'antipaywall/ideas';
---

<Platform title="Make your first open-source contribution" description="A guided first pull request: add an open-source tool you wish existed to the Antipaywall ideas repository, with your coding agent or right in the browser.">
  <section class="wrap pf-hero">
    <div class="pf-hero-main">
      <h1 class="pf-title">Your first open-source contribution</h1>
      <p class="lede fc-lede">
        Everyone's first pull request is a little nerve-wracking. This one is safe to get wrong: you'll add one small file, an
        open-source tool you wish existed, to Antipaywall's public ideas repository. Someone reviews it, and once it's merged it
        shows up on the site with your name on it. About ten minutes.
      </p>
      <div class="fc-progress" aria-hidden="true"><span data-fc-bar></span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap pf-section fc" data-fc data-repo={REPO}>
    <ol class="fc-steps">
      <li class="fc-step" data-step="1">
        <h2 class="pf-h3"><span class="osr-num">1</span> Pick something you wish existed</h2>
        <p>Something you pay for and wish had a free, open-source version, or a tool that doesn't exist at all. A rough idea is fine.</p>
        <div class="fc-fields">
          <label>What should it be called? <input class="input" data-fc-title type="text" maxlength="80" placeholder="Open-source review widget" /></label>
          <label>One line: what would it do? <input class="input" data-fc-pitch type="text" maxlength="140" placeholder="Pull Google and Yelp reviews into one widget for static sites" /></label>
          <label>Does it replace a paid tool? <span class="muted">(optional)</span> <input class="input" data-fc-replaces type="text" maxlength="60" placeholder="Elfsight" /></label>
        </div>
        <button class="key key-sm" type="button" data-fc-done="1">Next</button>
      </li>

      <li class="fc-step" data-step="2">
        <h2 class="pf-h3"><span class="osr-num">2</span> This is the file you'll add</h2>
        <p>Every idea is one Markdown file in the <code>ideas/</code> folder. The part between the <code>---</code> lines is for the site to read; the rest is for people.</p>
        <p class="muted small">File: <code data-fc-path>ideas/your-idea.md</code></p>
        <pre class="pf-code fc-file" data-fc-file></pre>
        <button class="key key-sm" type="button" data-fc-done="2">Next</button>
      </li>

      <li class="fc-step" data-step="3">
        <h2 class="pf-h3"><span class="osr-num">3</span> Make the change</h2>
        <p>Pick one way. Both end in the same place: a pull request, which is a proposal to add your change.</p>
        <div class="fc-ways">
          <div class="fc-way">
            <h3>In your browser, nothing to install</h3>
            <ol>
              <li>Sign in to GitHub.</li>
              <li>Press the button below. GitHub opens the new file with your text already in it.</li>
              <li>GitHub will say you can't edit this repository directly and offer to make your own copy (a <em>fork</em>). That's expected: say yes.</li>
              <li>Scroll down, press <b>Propose changes</b>.</li>
            </ol>
            <a class="key key-sm key-mint" data-fc-github href={`https://github.com/${REPO}`} rel="noopener" target="_blank">Open the file on GitHub</a>
          </div>
          <div class="fc-way">
            <h3>With your coding agent</h3>
            <p>Paste this into Claude Code, Cursor, Codex or another agent. It needs the <code>gh</code> command, signed in.</p>
            <pre class="pf-code fc-prompt" data-fc-prompt></pre>
            <button class="key key-sm key-milk" type="button" data-fc-copy>Copy the prompt</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <button class="key key-sm" type="button" data-fc-done="3">I've made the change</button>
      </li>

      <li class="fc-step" data-step="4">
        <h2 class="pf-h3"><span class="osr-num">4</span> Open the pull request</h2>
        <ul class="osr-how">
          <li><b>Title:</b> say what it adds: <code data-fc-prtitle>Add idea: …</code></li>
          <li><b>Description:</b> a sentence on why you want it. Mention anything you looked at that came close.</li>
          <li>Press <b>Create pull request</b>. That's it: you've proposed a change to an open-source project.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="muted">What happens next: a maintainer reads it, may ask a question or suggest a tweak (that's normal, not a rejection), and merges it. You'll get a GitHub notification at each step.</p>
        <button class="key key-sm" type="button" data-fc-done="4">I opened it</button>
      </li>

      <li class="fc-step" data-step="5">
        <h2 class="pf-h3"><span class="osr-num">5</span> You're an open-source contributor</h2>
        <p>The same steps work on any project: find something small, make the change, open a pull request, answer questions kindly.</p>
        <ul class="ob-steps">
          <li><a href="/explore"><b>Find a good first issue</b><span>Open-source projects that have said they want help.</span></a></li>
          <li><a href="/help-build"><b>Help build Antipaywall</b><span>The platform itself is open source too.</span></a></li>
          <li><a href="/open-source-ready"><b>Share your own project</b><span>The free guide to getting it ready.</span></a></li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</Platform>

<script>
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fc]');
  if (root) {
    const repo = root.dataset.repo!;
    const $ = <T extends Element>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s);
    const title = $<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fc-title]')!;
    const pitch = $<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fc-pitch]')!;
    const replaces = $<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fc-replaces]')!;
    const KEY = 'fc-progress-v1';
    const read = () => {
      try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY) ?? '{}'); } catch { return {}; }
    };
    const write = (v: object) => {
      try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify(v)); } catch { /* private window: fine */ }
    };
    const saved = read();
    title.value = saved.title ?? '';
    pitch.value = saved.pitch ?? '';
    replaces.value = saved.replaces ?? '';
    let done: number = saved.done ?? 0;

    const slugify = (s: string) => s.toLowerCase().normalize('NFKD').replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '').slice(0, 60) || 'my-idea';
    const yamlStr = (s: string) => JSON.stringify(s);
    const render = () => {
      const t = title.value.trim() || 'My idea';
      const p = pitch.value.trim();
      const r = replaces.value.trim();
      const slug = slugify(t);
      const file = [
        '---',
        `title: ${yamlStr(t)}`,
        ...(p ? [`pitch: ${yamlStr(p)}`] : []),
        'status: wanted',
        ...(r ? ['replaces:', `  - ${yamlStr(r)}`] : []),
        '---',
        '',
        '## The problem',
        '',
        p || 'What this would solve, in a sentence or two.',
        '',
        '## What it should do',
        '',
        '- The one thing it must do well',
        '',
      ].join('\n');
      $('[data-fc-path]')!.textContent = `ideas/${slug}.md`;
      $('[data-fc-file]')!.textContent = file;
      $('[data-fc-prtitle]')!.textContent = `Add idea: ${t}`;
      const gh = $<HTMLAnchorElement>('[data-fc-github]')!;
      gh.href = `https://github.com/${repo}/new/main/ideas?filename=${encodeURIComponent(`${slug}.md`)}&value=${encodeURIComponent(file)}`;
      $('[data-fc-prompt]')!.textContent =
        `I'd like to make my first open-source contribution. Fork ${repo} with gh, add the file ideas/${slug}.md with exactly this content, ` +
        `commit it with the message "Add idea: ${t}", push it to my fork, and open a pull request to ${repo} with the title "Add idea: ${t}". ` +
        `Explain each step to me as you go, and ask me before you push or open the pull request.\n\n${file}`;
      write({ title: title.value, pitch: pitch.value, replaces: replaces.value, done });
    };
    const show = () => {
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.fc-step').forEach((el) => {
        const n = Number(el.dataset.step);
        el.classList.toggle('is-done', n <= done);
        el.classList.toggle('is-current', n === done + 1);
      });
      const bar = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fc-bar]');
      if (bar) bar.style.width = `${Math.min(100, (done / 4) * 100)}%`;
    };
    [title, pitch, replaces].forEach((i) => i.addEventListener('input', render));
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-fc-done]').forEach((b) =>
      b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        done = Math.max(done, Number(b.dataset.fcDone));
        render();
        show();
        root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-step="${done + 1}"]`)?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'start' });
      }),
    );
    $('[data-fc-copy]')?.addEventListener('click', async (e) => {
      const btn = e.currentTarget as HTMLButtonElement;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText($('[data-fc-prompt]')!.textContent ?? '');
        btn.textContent = 'Copied';
      } catch {
        btn.textContent = 'Select the text and copy it';
      }
    });
    render();
    show();
  }
</script>
